 5. 🍁 Trump&#x27;s new Canada ban 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A truck crosses into the U.S. on the new Gordie Howe International Bridge connecting Detroit and Windsor, Ontario. Photo: Jeff Kowalsky/AFP via Getty Images President Trump said the U.S. will ban Canadian alcohol, some dairy products and large motorcycles, sharply escalating a trade war largely fought with tariffs, Axios' Courtenay Brown writes. 

 Why it matters: The measures deepen the economic rift between countries that have spent decades interlinking commerce, threatening disruption for businesses and consumers on both sides of the border. The import bans take effect Sept. 29, effectively cutting off U.S. market access for the targeted Canadian goods rather than simply making them more expensive.

 The White House said it'll also expand the existing 50% tariffs to dozens of additional Canadian products — including some steel and aluminum goods, furniture and paper — effective Sept. 15 (next Tuesday). Keep reading . 

 
 
