 7. 📱 Coming today: Apple&#x27;s first foldable phone 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Shoshana Gordon/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Apple will unveil its first foldable iPhone today (1 p.m. ET) — the biggest single design change in the device's nearly 20-year lifespan, Bloomberg Apple guru Mark Gurman writes . 

 The $2,000+ product emerged from years of internal debate. Early concepts focused on a foldable iPad rather than an iPhone. Tim Cook, better known for his command of finance and supply chains, personally pushed the project toward a phone after watching foldables take off in Asia. "Tim was the earliest and biggest champion of this," an Apple insider said. The announcement will be the public debut of new CEO John Ternus, who replaced Tim Cook on Sept. 1.

 Go deeper : Apple's foldable iPhone was a decade in the making (Bloomberg gift link). 
 
