 8. 🏈 1 for the road: Football America 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Gallup . Chart: Noah Bressner/Axios The NFL season starts tonight — Patriots at Seahawks, 8:20 p.m. ET on NBC — with football by far the country's favorite sport to watch, according to a Gallup poll released this morning.

 The catch: The 31% share of Americans who named football as their favorite is the lowest since 2001. 🧮 By the numbers: Soccer just hit its highest-ever share (9%) in Gallup's polling on the question, which dates back to 1937.

 The sport is closing in on basketball (11%) and baseball (10%). Photo: Quinn Rooney/Getty Images 🦘 Above: The San Francisco 49ers practice in Melbourne, Australia, before their game tomorrow night (8:35 p.m. ET, Netflix ) against the L.A. Rams at the Melbourne Cricket Ground — the first regular-season NFL game Down Under. 

